[E0449] Error: `into` keeps `self` in `out`, and its signature does not say it does
    ╭─[ err/460_kept_through_a_reference/main.wip:20:9 ]
    │
 19 │     fn into(out: &var Option<Seen>) = {
    │     ─┬
    │      ╰── `self` is not in `keeps`
 20 │         out = .Some(Seen(name: &self.name))
    │               ──────────────┬──────────────
    │                             ╰──────────────── keeps what `self` holds or borrows
    │
    │ Help: say that `into` keeps `self`
    │
    │ Note: a call keeps nothing of its arguments but what its `keeps` names, so that its callers know what stays borrowed
────╯
